    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2GMLutc9BCfRWbTmX5KGgDe)_\n\nDoc only: `docs/architecture/svg-tag-mode-in-stages.org`. No code changes.\n\n- Stage 1: Rougier's `svg-tag-mode` unmodified, installed with `use-package` + Elpaca `:ensure`, off by default, no hook.\n- Stage 2 (sub-stages 2a–2e): the tag rendering from #254/#260/#264 (group colours, emoji, theme palette), each its own PR with a gate.\n- What #254/#259/#260/#264 did, what to keep and what not to repeat.\n- Does SVG hang Emacs? No evidence it did (the hang was vulpea autosync work, and `svg-tag-mode` ran on `prog-mode` before without trouble), plus the cost points read from the `svg-tag-mode`/`svg-lib` source and seven hypotheses to measure.\n- Testing and debugging checklist for the Mac: graphic frame checks, batch checks, toggling, profiling, memory, `C-g` with `debug-on-quit`, `SIGUSR2`, `sample`, bisecting, stage gates.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container). Claims about Emacs internals I did not check in source are marked _(memory)_ in the doc.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAqGFajtL2M2WMoWD9)_",
